      "attribute": "immunosuppression context",
      "direction": "supports_X",
      "evidence_refs": ["independent_blind_observation"],
      "value": "Heart transplant + pacemaker implies chronic immunosuppression; PTLD is a well-established complication in this setting, often presenting as asymptomatic pulmonary nodules."
    },
    {
      "attribute": "nodule morphology on CT",
      "direction": "supports_both",
      "evidence_refs": ["image_4", "image_5", "independent_blind_observation"],
      "value": "Two discrete, solid, well-circumscribed, non-cavitary, non-spiculated nodules—morphology compatible with both PTLD and fungal granulomas (e.g., histoplasmosis, coccidioidomycosis), though fungal lesions more commonly show calcification or cavitation in chronic cases."
    },
    {
      "attribute": "absence of symptoms and geographic exposure",
      "direction": "supports_X",
      "evidence_refs": ["question"],
      "value": "PTLD can be indolent and asymptomatic; fungal infections (other than blastomycosis) typically require endemic exposure (e.g., Ohio/Mississippi river valleys for histoplasmosis, SW US for coccidioidomycosis); absence of such exposure weakens Y."
    },
    {
      "attribute": "radiographic report vs visual evidence",
      "direction": "conflict",
      "evidence_refs": ["observation_2", "independent_blind_observation"],
      "value": "The formal X-ray report (observation_2) states 'lungs are clear without focal consolidation', contradicting the visual presence of two nodules on image_1 and confirmed on CT (images_4–5). This discrepancy suggests the report may be outdated or misaligned with the images; visual evidence takes precedence per instructions.
    },
    {
      "attribute": "tool diagnostic output",
      "direction": "unresolved",
      "evidence_refs": ["observation_3"],
      "value": "One tool returned 'Pneumonia', which is inconsistent with asymptomatic presentation and nodule morphology; this output is likely erroneous and not supported by imaging."
    }
  ],
  "needs_followup": true,
  "followup_question": "Are the pulmonary nodules calcified on high-resolution CT?"
}

